IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2020, subsections (o) to (x).
-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively). Same reading of results as snap4-s2020-a-d.l4: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING.
-- The text is the converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.
-- Dates of the Act are `Date day month year`. A period of months is counted with the daydate library's `add months`.

§ `s 2020(o) Data processing systems; model plan; State plans; evaluation and report to Congress; time for implementation`

DECLARE `s 2020(o)(1) element of the model plan` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(o)(1) intake procedures`
    `s 2020(o)(1) eligibility determinations and calculation of benefits`
    `s 2020(o)(1) verification procedures`
    `s 2020(o)(1) coordination with related Federal and State programs`
    `s 2020(o)(1) the issuance of benefits`
    `s 2020(o)(1) reconciliation procedures`
    `s 2020(o)(1) the generation of notices`
    `s 2020(o)(1) program reporting`
    `s 2020(o)(1) any other element`

-- src:1587 | The Secretary shall develop, after consultation with, and with the assistance of, an advisory group of State agencies appointed by the Secretary without regard to the provisions of chapter 10 of title 5, a model plan for the comprehensive automation of data processing and computerization of information systems under the supplemental nutrition assistance program. …
-- jural: State agencies | the Secretary | claim and duty: a model plan for comprehensive automation, developed with an advisory group of State agencies
@ref s 2020(o)(1) (src:1587)
GIVEN `the Secretary has consulted, and had the assistance of, an advisory group of State agencies appointed by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(o)(1) the model plan is developed as the text requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has consulted, and had the assistance of, an advisory group of State agencies appointed by the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after consultation with, and with the assistance of, an advisory group of State agencies appointed by the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1587 | The plan shall be developed and made available for public comment through publication of the proposed plan in the Federal Register not later than October 1, 1986. …
@ref s 2020(o)(1) (src:1587)
GIVEN `the day the proposed plan was published in the Federal Register` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A date test: TRUE on 1 October 1986, FALSE on 2 October 1986. A spent deadline, encoded because the text states it.
`s 2020(o)(1) the proposed plan was published by the deadline` MEANS
    `the day the proposed plan was published in the Federal Register` AT MOST (Date 1 10 1986)

-- src:1587 | The Secretary shall complete the plan, taking into consideration public comments received, not later than February 1, 1987. …
@ref s 2020(o)(1) (src:1587)
GIVEN `the day the Secretary completed the plan` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A date test: TRUE on 1 February 1987, FALSE on 2 February 1987.
`s 2020(o)(1) the plan was completed by the deadline` MEANS
    `the day the Secretary completed the plan` AT MOST (Date 1 2 1987)

-- src:1587 | The elements of the plan may include intake procedures, eligibility determinations and calculation of benefits, verification procedures, coordination with related Federal and State programs, the issuance of benefits, reconciliation procedures, the generation of notices, and program reporting. In developing the plan, the Secretary shall take into account automated data processing and information systems already in existence in States and shall provide for consistency with such systems.
@ref s 2020(o)(1) (src:1587)
GIVEN `the element` IS A `s 2020(o)(1) element of the model plan`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(o)(1) the plan may include the element` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the element`
    WHEN `s 2020(o)(1) any other element` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The elements of the plan may include"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1587 | In developing the plan, the Secretary shall take into account automated data processing and information systems already in existence in States and shall provide for consistency with such systems.
@ref s 2020(o)(1) (src:1587)
GIVEN `the system is an automated data processing or information system already in existence in the States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(o)(1) the Secretary must take the system into account and provide for consistency with it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the system is an automated data processing or information system already in existence in the States` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "automated data processing and information systems already in existence in States"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1588 | Not later than October 1, 1987, each State agency shall develop and submit to the Secretary for approval a plan for the use of an automated data processing and information retrieval system to administer the supplemental nutrition assistance program in such State. The State plan shall take into consideration the model plan developed by the Secretary under paragraph (1) and shall provide time frames for completion of various phases of the State plan. If a State agency already has a sufficient automated data processing and information retrieval system, the State plan may, subject to the Secretary’s approval, reflect the existing State system.
@ref s 2020(o)(2) (src:1588)
GIVEN `the day the State agency submitted its plan` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A date test: TRUE on 1 October 1987, FALSE on 2 October 1987.
`s 2020(o)(2) the State plan was submitted by the deadline` MEANS
    `the day the State agency submitted its plan` AT MOST (Date 1 10 1987)

-- src:1588 | If a State agency already has a sufficient automated data processing and information retrieval system, the State plan may, subject to the Secretary’s approval, reflect the existing State system.
@ref s 2020(o)(2) (src:1588)
GIVEN `the State agency already has a sufficient automated data processing and information retrieval system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary approves` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(o)(2) the State plan may reflect the existing State system` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State agency already has a sufficient automated data processing and information retrieval system`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a State agency already has a sufficient automated data processing and information retrieval system, the State plan may, subject to the Secretary's approval, reflect the existing State system"
        IF `the Secretary approves` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the Secretary's approval"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1589 | Not later than April 1, 1988, the Secretary shall prepare and submit to Congress an evaluation of the degree and sufficiency of each State’s automated data processing and computerized information systems for the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program, including State plans submitted under paragraph (2). Such report shall include an analysis of additional steps needed for States to achieve effective and cost-efficient data processing and information systems. The Secretary, thereafter, shall periodically update such report.
@ref s 2020(o)(3) (src:1589)
GIVEN `the day the Secretary submitted the evaluation to Congress` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A date test: TRUE on 1 April 1988, FALSE on 2 April 1988.
`s 2020(o)(3) the evaluation was submitted by the deadline` MEANS
    `the day the Secretary submitted the evaluation to Congress` AT MOST (Date 1 4 1988)

-- src:1589 | The Secretary, thereafter, shall periodically update such report.
@ref s 2020(o)(3) (src:1589)
GIVEN `the evaluation has been submitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(o)(3) the Secretary must periodically update the report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the evaluation has been submitted` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "thereafter"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1590 | (4) Based on the Secretary’s findings in such report submitted under paragraph (3), the Secretary may require a State agency, as necessary to rectify identified shortcomings in the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in the State, except where such direction would displace State initiatives already under way, to take specified steps to automate data processing systems or computerize information systems for the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in the State if the Secretary finds that, in the absence of such systems, there will be program accountability or integrity problems that will substantially affect the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in the State.
-- jural: the State agency | the Secretary | power and liability: the Secretary may require specified steps to automate, within the stated limits
@ref s 2020(o)(4) (src:1590)
GIVEN `the Secretary's findings in the report under paragraph (3) show shortcomings and the steps are necessary to rectify them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction would displace State initiatives already under way` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary finds that, in the absence of such systems, there will be program accountability or integrity problems that will substantially affect the administration of the program in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(o)(4) the Secretary may require the State agency to take specified steps to automate or computerize` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the direction would displace State initiatives already under way`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where such direction would displace State initiatives already under way"
        IF NOT `the Secretary finds that, in the absence of such systems, there will be program accountability or integrity problems that will substantially affect the administration of the program in the State`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Secretary finds that, in the absence of such systems, there will be program accountability or integrity problems that will substantially affect the administration"
        IF `the Secretary's findings in the report under paragraph (3) show shortcomings and the steps are necessary to rectify them` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Based on the Secretary's findings in such report submitted under paragraph (3), ... as necessary to rectify identified shortcomings"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1592 | (A) Subject to subparagraph (B), in the case of a plan for an automated data processing and information retrieval system submitted by a State agency to the Secretary under paragraph (2), such State agency shall—
-- src:1593 | (i) commence implementation of its plan not later than October 1, 1988; and
-- src:1594 | (ii) meet the time frames set forth in the plan.
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agency | claim and duty: implementation commences by 1 October 1988 and meets the plan's time frames, unless the Secretary extends the deadline
@ref s 2020(o)(5)(A) (src:1592-1594)
GIVEN `the extension of the deadline the Secretary has granted, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2020(o)(5)(A) the day by which the State agency must commence implementation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the extension of the deadline the Secretary has granted, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN Date 1 10 1988
    WHEN JUST extended THEN extended

@ref s 2020(o)(5)(A)(i) (src:1593)
GIVEN `the day the State agency commenced implementation of its plan` IS A DATE
      `the extension of the deadline the Secretary has granted, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A date test against the deadline above: TRUE on 1 October 1988 with no extension, FALSE on 2 October 1988.
`s 2020(o)(5)(A)(i) implementation was commenced by the deadline` MEANS
    `the day the State agency commenced implementation of its plan` AT MOST (`s 2020(o)(5)(A) the day by which the State agency must commence implementation` `the extension of the deadline the Secretary has granted, if any`)

-- src:1595 | (B) The Secretary shall extend a deadline imposed under subparagraph (A) to the extent the Secretary deems appropriate based on the Secretary’s finding of a good faith effort of a State agency to implement its plan in accordance with subparagraph (A).
-- jural: the State agency | the Secretary | claim and duty: the deadline is extended to the extent the Secretary deems appropriate on a finding of good faith effort
@ref s 2020(o)(5)(B) (src:1595)
GIVEN `the Secretary finds a good faith effort of the State agency to implement its plan in accordance with subparagraph (A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(o)(5)(B) the Secretary must extend the deadline to the extent the Secretary deems appropriate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary finds a good faith effort of the State agency to implement its plan in accordance with subparagraph (A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "based on the Secretary's finding of a good faith effort of a State agency"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(p) to (r) State verification, prisoners, deceased individuals`

DECLARE `s 2020(p) verification system` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(p) an immigration status verification system established under section 1137 of the Social Security Act`
    `s 2020(p) an income and eligibility verification system in accordance with standards set by the Secretary`
    `s 2020(p) any other system`

-- src:1597 | In carrying out the supplemental nutrition assistance program, a State agency shall be required to use an immigration status verification system established under section 1137 of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1320b–7), and an income and eligibility verification system, in accordance with standards set by the Secretary.
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agency | claim and duty: the State agency must use the two verification systems
@ref s 2020(p) (src:1597)
GIVEN `the system` IS A `s 2020(p) verification system`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(p) the State agency must be required to use the system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the system`
    WHEN `s 2020(p) any other system` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names two systems and nothing else
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1599 | The Secretary shall assist States, to the maximum extent practicable, in implementing a system to conduct computer matches or other systems to prevent prisoners described in subsection (e)(18)(B) from participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of any household.
-- jural: States | the Secretary | claim and duty: assistance in implementing computer matches to prevent prisoners from participating
@ref s 2020(q) (src:1599)
GIVEN `the State is implementing a system to conduct computer matches or other systems to prevent prisoners described in subsection (e)(18)(B) from participating as a member of any household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assistance is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(q) the Secretary must assist the State` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State is implementing a system to conduct computer matches or other systems to prevent prisoners described in subsection (e)(18)(B) from participating as a member of any household` AND `assistance is practicable` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the maximum extent practicable, in implementing a system to conduct computer matches or other systems"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(r) step` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(r)(1) enter into a cooperative arrangement with the Commissioner of Social Security to obtain information on individuals who are deceased`
    `s 2020(r)(2) use the information to verify and otherwise ensure that benefits are not issued to individuals who are deceased`
    `s 2020(r) any other step`

-- src:1601 | Each State agency shall—
-- src:1602 | (1) enter into a cooperative arrangement with the Commissioner of Social Security, pursuant to the authority of the Commissioner under section 205(r)(3) of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 405(r)(3)), to obtain information on individuals who are deceased; and
-- src:1603 | (2) use the information to verify and otherwise ensure that benefits are not issued to individuals who are deceased.
-- jural: the public fisc | each State agency | claim and duty: no benefits are issued to a deceased individual
@ref s 2020(r) (src:1601-1603)
GIVEN `the step` IS A `s 2020(r) step`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(r) the State agency must take the step` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `s 2020(r) any other step` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names two steps and nothing else
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 2020(s) Transitional benefits option`

-- inert: 1604 | reason 1 | the subsection heading (s) "Transitional benefits option"

-- src:1606 | A State agency may provide transitional supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits—
-- src:1607 | (A) to a household that ceases to receive cash assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.); or
-- src:1608 | (B) at the option of the State, to a household with children that ceases to receive cash assistance under a State-funded public assistance program.
-- jural: a household that ceases to receive cash assistance | the State agency | privilege and no-right: the State agency may provide transitional benefits
@ref s 2020(s)(1) (src:1606-1608)
GIVEN `the household ceases to receive cash assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household has children and ceases to receive cash assistance under a State-funded public assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State has opted to provide transitional benefits to such households` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(s)(1) the State agency may provide transitional benefits to the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household ceases to receive cash assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the household has children and ceases to receive cash assistance under a State-funded public assistance program` AND `the State has opted to provide transitional benefits to such households` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(B) at the option of the State, to a household with children that ceases to receive cash assistance under a State-funded public assistance program"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1610 | Under paragraph (1), a household may receive transitional supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for a period of not more than 5 months after the date on which cash assistance is terminated.
-- jural: the household | the State agency | privilege: transitional benefits for not more than 5 months after cash assistance ends
-- fork: F-1 | 1609-1610 | "not more than 5 months after the date on which cash assistance is terminated": chosen reading, the period runs to the same day of the month five months on, and that last day is counted; the other reading ends it the day before
@ref s 2020(s)(2) (src:1610)
GIVEN `the day cash assistance is terminated` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A period test, and the answer to the keel's field `the period or the contact falls within a transitional benefit period under section 2020(s)`:
-- the day is after the termination and not later than the same day five months on (the last day is counted: fork F-1).
`s 2020(s)(2) the day falls within the transitional benefits period` MEANS
    `the day` GREATER THAN `the day cash assistance is terminated` AND `the day` AT MOST (`add months` `the day cash assistance is terminated` 5)

@ref s 2020(s)(2) (src:1610)
GIVEN `the day cash assistance is terminated` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(s)(2) the household may receive transitional benefits on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day` AT MOST `the day cash assistance is terminated` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after the date on which cash assistance is terminated"
        IF `the day` AT MOST (`add months` `the day cash assistance is terminated` 5) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than 5 months after the date on which cash assistance is terminated"

-- src:1612 | During the transitional benefits period under paragraph (2), a household shall receive an amount of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits equal to the allotment received in the month immediately preceding the date on which cash assistance was terminated, adjusted for the change in household income as a result of—
-- src:1613 | (A) the termination of cash assistance; and
-- src:1614 | (B) at the option of the State agency, information from another program in which the household participates.
-- jural: the household | the State agency | claim and duty: an amount equal to the last allotment before cash assistance ended, adjusted for the change in income
@ref s 2020(s)(3) (src:1612-1614)
GIVEN `the allotment received in the month immediately preceding the date on which cash assistance was terminated, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the change in the allotment from the termination of cash assistance, in dollars (negative if it falls)` IS A NUMBER
      `the State agency has opted to take information from another program into account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change in the allotment from that information, in dollars (negative if it falls)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- A sum fixed by the text; the two changes are computed under the Act's other sections and are supplied. A negative total is not corrected here: the text does not say.
`s 2020(s)(3) the amount of transitional benefits` MEANS
    `the allotment received in the month immediately preceding the date on which cash assistance was terminated, in dollars`
        PLUS `the change in the allotment from the termination of cash assistance, in dollars (negative if it falls)`
        PLUS (IF `the State agency has opted to take information from another program into account` THEN `the change in the allotment from that information, in dollars (negative if it falls)` ELSE 0)

DECLARE `s 2020(s)(4) step in the final month` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(s)(4)(A) require the household to cooperate in a recertification of eligibility`
    `s 2020(s)(4)(B) initiate a new certification period without regard to whether the preceding certification period has expired`
    `s 2020(s)(4) any other step`

-- src:1616 | In the final month of the transitional benefits period under paragraph (2), the State agency may—
-- src:1617 | (A) require the household to cooperate in a recertification of eligibility; and
-- src:1618 | (B) initiate a new certification period for the household without regard to whether the preceding certification period has expired.
-- jural: the household | the State agency | power and liability: recertification or a new certification period in the final month
@ref s 2020(s)(4) (src:1616-1618)
GIVEN `it is the final month of the transitional benefits period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the step` IS A `s 2020(s)(4) step in the final month`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(s)(4) the State agency may take the step` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is the final month of the transitional benefits period` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the final month of the transitional benefits period"
        IF `the step` EQUALS `s 2020(s)(4) any other step` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names two steps and nothing else
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1620 | A household shall not be eligible for transitional benefits under this subsection if the household—
-- src:1621 | (A) loses eligibility under section 2015 of this title;
-- src:1622 | (B) is sanctioned for a failure to perform an action required by Federal, State, or local law relating to a cash assistance program described in paragraph (1); or
-- src:1623 | (C) is a member of any other category of households designated by the State agency as ineligible for transitional benefits.
-- jural: the State agency | the household | disability: no transitional benefits to a household that loses eligibility, is sanctioned, or is in a category the State designates
@ref s 2020(s)(5) (src:1620-1623)
GIVEN `the household loses eligibility under section 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household is sanctioned for a failure to perform an action required by Federal, State, or local law relating to a cash assistance program described in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household is a member of a category of households designated by the State agency as ineligible for transitional benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(s)(5) the household is eligible for transitional benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household loses eligibility under section 2015` OR `the household is sanctioned for a failure to perform an action required by Federal, State, or local law relating to a cash assistance program described in paragraph (1)` OR `the household is a member of a category of households designated by the State agency as ineligible for transitional benefits`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A household shall not be eligible for transitional benefits under this subsection if the household"
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the limitation takes eligibility away and grants none; paragraph (1) says who may be given transitional benefits
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1626 | A household receiving transitional benefits under this subsection may apply for recertification at any time during the transitional benefits period under paragraph (2).
-- jural: a household receiving transitional benefits | the State agency | claim and duty: it may apply for recertification at any time in the period
@ref s 2020(s)(6)(A) (src:1626)
GIVEN `the household is receiving transitional benefits under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day applied falls within the transitional benefits period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(s)(6)(A) the household may apply for recertification` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is receiving transitional benefits under this subsection` AND `the day applied falls within the transitional benefits period` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A household receiving transitional benefits under this subsection may apply for recertification at any time during the transitional benefits period"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1628 | If a household applies for recertification under subparagraph (A), the allotment of the household for all subsequent months shall be determined without regard to this subsection.
-- jural: the household | the State agency | claim and duty: the allotment for all subsequent months is determined without regard to subsection (s)
@ref s 2020(s)(6)(B) (src:1628)
GIVEN `the household applies for recertification under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(s)(6)(B) the allotment for all subsequent months is determined without regard to this subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household applies for recertification under subparagraph (A)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a household applies for recertification under subparagraph (A)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(t) Grants for simplified application and eligibility determination systems and improved access to benefits`

-- src:1631 | Subject to the availability of appropriations under section 2027(a) of this title, for each fiscal year, the Secretary shall use not more than $5,000,000 of funds made available under section 2027(a)(1) of this title to make grants to pay 100 percent of the costs of eligible entities approved by the Secretary to carry out projects to develop and implement supplemental nutrition assistance program simplified application and eligibility determination systems.
-- jural: eligible entities | the Secretary | power: grants of up to $5,000,000 a fiscal year, paying 100 percent of costs
@ref s 2020(t)(1) (src:1631)
GIVEN `the amount the Secretary uses in the fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(t)(1) the Secretary may use the amount for grants` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount the Secretary uses in the fiscal year, in dollars` AT MOST 5000000 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary shall use not more than $5,000,000 of funds made available under section 2027(a)(1)"

-- src:1631 | to make grants to pay 100 percent of the costs of eligible entities approved by the Secretary to carry out projects to develop and implement supplemental nutrition assistance program simplified application and eligibility determination systems.
@ref s 2020(t)(1) (src:1631)
GIVEN `the costs of the approved eligible entity's project, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- A sum fixed by the text: the grant pays 100 percent of the costs.
`s 2020(t)(1) the grant` MEANS `the costs of the approved eligible entity's project, in dollars` TIMES 100%

DECLARE `s 2020(t)(2) activity` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(t)(2)(A) coordinating application and eligibility determination processes, including verification practices, with other Federal, State, and local assistance programs`
    `s 2020(t)(2)(B) establishing enhanced technological methods that improve the administrative infrastructure used in processing applications and determining eligibility`
    `s 2020(t)(2)(C) carrying out such other activities as the Secretary determines to be appropriate`
    `s 2020(t)(2) any other activity`

-- src:1633 | A project under paragraph (1) may consist of—
-- src:1634 | (A) coordinating application and eligibility determination processes, including verification practices, under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and other Federal, State, and local assistance programs;
-- src:1635 | (B) establishing enhanced technological methods that improve the administrative infrastructure used in processing applications and determining eligibility; or
-- src:1636 | (C) carrying out such other activities as the Secretary determines to be appropriate.
-- jural: eligible entities | the Secretary | privilege and no-right: the projects a grant may support
@ref s 2020(t)(2) (src:1633-1636)
GIVEN `the activity` IS A `s 2020(t)(2) activity`
      `the Secretary determines that the other activities are appropriate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(t)(2) the project may consist of the activity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `s 2020(t)(2)(A) coordinating application and eligibility determination processes, including verification practices, with other Federal, State, and local assistance programs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2020(t)(2)(B) establishing enhanced technological methods that improve the administrative infrastructure used in processing applications and determining eligibility` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2020(t)(2)(C) carrying out such other activities as the Secretary determines to be appropriate` THEN
        IF `the Secretary determines that the other activities are appropriate` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such other activities as the Secretary determines to be appropriate"
    WHEN `s 2020(t)(2) any other activity` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "A project under paragraph (1) may consist of"

-- src:1638 | A grant under this subsection shall not be made for the ongoing cost of carrying out any project.
-- jural: the Secretary | eligible entities | disability: no grant for the ongoing cost of a project
@ref s 2020(t)(3) (src:1638)
GIVEN `the cost is the ongoing cost of carrying out a project` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(t)(3) a grant may be made for the cost` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the cost is the ongoing cost of carrying out a project`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A grant under this subsection shall not be made for the ongoing cost of carrying out any project"
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text bars the ongoing cost and says nothing of other costs
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(t)(4) entity` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(t)(4)(A) a State agency administering the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
    `s 2020(t)(4)(B) a State or local government`
    `s 2020(t)(4)(C) an agency providing health or welfare services`
    `s 2020(t)(4)(D) a public health or educational entity`
    `s 2020(t)(4)(E) a private nonprofit entity such as a community-based organization, food bank, or other emergency feeding organization`
    `s 2020(t)(4) an entity of none of those kinds`

-- src:1640 | To be eligible to receive a grant under this subsection, an entity shall be—
-- src:1641 | (A) a State agency administering the supplemental nutrition assistance program;
-- src:1642 | (B) a State or local government;
-- src:1643 | (C) an agency providing health or welfare services;
-- src:1644 | (D) a public health or educational entity; or
-- src:1645 | (E) a private nonprofit entity such as a community-based organization, food bank, or other emergency feeding organization.
-- jural: an entity | the Secretary | power and liability: only five kinds of entity are eligible to receive a grant
@ref s 2020(t)(4) (src:1640-1645)
GIVEN `the entity` IS A `s 2020(t)(4) entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(t)(4) the entity is eligible to receive a grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entity`
    WHEN `s 2020(t)(4) an entity of none of those kinds` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To be eligible to receive a grant under this subsection, an entity shall be"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1646 | (5) Selection of eligible entities
