§ `s 2020(v) Data exchange standards for improved interoperability`

DECLARE `s 2020(v)(1) subject of the standards` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(v)(1)(A) necessary categories of information that State agencies operating related programs are required to electronically exchange with another State agency`
    `s 2020(v)(1)(B) Federal reporting and data exchange required under applicable law`
    `s 2020(v)(1) any other subject`

-- src:1659 | The Secretary shall, in consultation with an interagency work group established by the Office of Management and Budget, and considering State government perspectives, designate data exchange standards to govern, under this chapter—
-- src:1660 | (A) necessary categories of information that State agencies operating related programs are required under applicable law to electronically exchange with another State agency; and
-- src:1661 | (B) Federal reporting and data exchange required under applicable law.
-- jural: State agencies | the Secretary | claim and duty: data exchange standards designated to govern the exchange
@ref s 2020(v)(1) (src:1659-1661)
GIVEN `the subject` IS A `s 2020(v)(1) subject of the standards`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(v)(1) the Secretary must designate data exchange standards to govern the subject` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the subject`
    WHEN `s 2020(v)(1) any other subject` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names two subjects
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 2020(v)(2) requirement of the standards` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(v)(2)(A) incorporate a widely accepted, nonproprietary, searchable, computer-readable format`
    `s 2020(v)(2)(B) contain interoperable standards developed and maintained by intergovernmental partnerships`
    `s 2020(v)(2)(C) incorporate interoperable standards developed and maintained by Federal entities with authority over contracting and financial assistance`
    `s 2020(v)(2)(D) be consistent with and implement applicable accounting principles`
    `s 2020(v)(2)(E) be implemented in a manner that is cost-effective and improves program efficiency and effectiveness`
    `s 2020(v)(2)(F) be capable of being continually upgraded as necessary`
    `s 2020(v)(2) any other requirement`

-- src:1663 | The data exchange standards required by paragraph (1) shall, to the maximum extent practicable—
-- src:1664 | (A) incorporate a widely accepted, nonproprietary, searchable, computer-readable format, such as the eXtensible Markup Language;
-- src:1665 | (B) contain interoperable standards developed and maintained by intergovernmental partnerships, such as the National Information Exchange Model;
-- src:1666 | (C) incorporate interoperable standards developed and maintained by Federal entities with authority over contracting and financial assistance;
-- src:1667 | (D) be consistent with and implement applicable accounting principles;
-- src:1668 | (E) be implemented in a manner that is cost-effective and improves program efficiency and effectiveness; and
-- src:1669 | (F) be capable of being continually upgraded as necessary.
@ref s 2020(v)(2) (src:1663-1669)
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `s 2020(v)(2) requirement of the standards`
      `it is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(v)(2) the data exchange standards must meet the requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirement` EQUALS `s 2020(v)(2) any other requirement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names six requirements
        IF `it is practicable` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the maximum extent practicable"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1671 | Nothing in this subsection requires a change to existing data exchange standards for Federal reporting found to be effective and efficient.
-- jural: States | the Secretary | immunity: no change is required to existing effective and efficient data exchange standards for Federal reporting
@ref s 2020(v)(3) (src:1671)
GIVEN `the existing data exchange standard for Federal reporting is found to be effective and efficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(v)(3) this subsection requires a change to the existing standard` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the existing data exchange standard for Federal reporting is found to be effective and efficient`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this subsection requires a change to existing data exchange standards for Federal reporting found to be effective and efficient"
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks only of standards found effective and efficient
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(w) Advice regarding employment and training services`

-- src:1673 | For households containing at least one adult, with no elderly or disabled members and with no earned income at their last certification or required report, a State agency shall, at the time of recertification, be required to advise members of the household not exempt under section 2015(d)(2) of this title regarding available employment and training services.
-- jural: the members of a household with an adult, no elderly or disabled member and no earned income | the State agency | claim and duty: advice about available employment and training services at recertification
@ref s 2020(w) (src:1673)
GIVEN `the number of adults in the household` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2012(j) the answers, member by member, to whether each member is an elderly or disabled member` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the household has earned income at its last certification or required report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the time of recertification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(d)(2) the member is exempt` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(w) the State agency must advise the member regarding available employment and training services` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of adults in the household` LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "households containing at least one adult"
        IF `the household has earned income at its last certification or required report` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with no earned income at their last certification or required report"
        IF NOT `it is the time of recertification` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the time of recertification"
        IF count (filter (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) `s 2012(j) the answers, member by member, to whether each member is an elderly or disabled member`) GREATER THAN 0 THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with no elderly or disabled members"
        IF count (filter (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS NOTHING) `s 2012(j) the answers, member by member, to whether each member is an elderly or disabled member`) GREATER THAN 0 THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a member is elderly or disabled is answered by section 2012(j)
        IF `s 2015(d)(2) the member is exempt` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "members of the household not exempt under section 2015(d)(2)" is answered by section 2015(d)(2)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(x) National Accuracy Clearinghouse`

-- src:1676 | In this subsection, the term “indication of multiple issuance” means an indication, based on a computer match, that supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits are being issued to an individual by more than 1 State agency simultaneously.
-- jural: none | none | none: a definition
@ref s 2020(x)(1) (src:1676)
GIVEN `the indication is based on a computer match` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of State agencies simultaneously issuing benefits to the individual` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(x)(1) the indication is an indication of multiple issuance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the indication is based on a computer match` AND `the number of State agencies simultaneously issuing benefits to the individual` GREATER THAN 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the term “indication of multiple issuance” means an indication, based on a computer match, that supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits are being issued to an individual by more than 1 State agency simultaneously"

